This PR does three things:

1) Prune dead variables. After focussing and splitting, fewer variables are live. The dead variables and their corresponding where clauses are now removed. This removal only happens if the `/pruneFunctionsAndAxioms` flag is set. It changes the behavior of the following program:
```
var x: int where false 

if (*) {
 assert x > 0;
 assert false;
} else {
 assume {:focus} true;
 assert false;
}
```

The code above generates two splits: one with only the `if` branch and another with only the `else` branch. But `x` is treated to be live in both because dead variable elimination is done before focussing/splitting. So, in the earlier version, Boogie determines that `x` is live, so it assumes the `where` clause of `x`. This means it inserts `assume false` **before** the `if` and both assertions prove. 

Now, if pruning is enabled, dead variables are recomputed. So, we determine the variable `x` to be dead in the `else` split and delete its where clause (`assume false`). This means the assertion in `else` fails when pruning is enabled.

2) Refactor `FindAttribute`: The code around finding attributes looked a bit clunky: it had for loops everywhere for iterating through the attributes. I have refactored  `FindAttribute` to take a `property: QKeyValue -> bool` function; it applies this function to every attribute and returns the first one that satisfies it. 

3) Compose focussing and splitting: I made a mistake in composing focussing and splitting earlier. Nothing unsound but it was generating more splits than necessary. I have fixed it and refactored the code a bit to make it cleaner.

When using an external ID (as opposed to an actual UNIVAF ID) in the `/api/edge/locations/<id>` endpoint, we are currently returning the `position` value as WKB. For example:

```js
// http://getmyvax.org/api/edge/locations/rite_aid:5610
{
  "data": {
    "id": "64d41035-6dcf-4331-a9f9-438dec46ee31",
    "position": "0101000020E6100000D122DBF97E7A5DC08716D9CEF7034140",
    // ...
  }
}
```

It looks like we introduced this bug in #147, and I noticed it while reviewing #304. This fixes it and adds coverage for it in tests.

This PR skips mass assignment protection if the data passed is an instance of `ValidatedData`.

It covers the following methods:

```php
Model::make();
Model::firstOrNew();
Model::firstOrCreate();
Model::updateOrCreate();
Model::create();
Model::forceCreate();
Model::fill();
Model::forceFill();
Model::update();
Model::updateQuietly();
```

Update:

Relationship methods (create, firstOrCreate, firstOrNew, updateOrCreate) will also accept `ValidatedData` data.

This PR adds the foundational blocks to the Data (and the SDK used to access that Data) needed to fix #85, which'll add support for both built-in/simple types (e.g. bool/int/float/string etc) and #81 (with Lists of Lists, or Dictionaries of Dictionaries)

For now this is limited in scope since this is changing primarily the Data layer - once this PR is in we can implement #85 and #81 within the Data layer and then look to support those within the Go SDK Generator and Importer too

Ultimately this changes the API response to return the Request/Response Object as an Object rather than just a model name, so that we can include the Type (e.g. Boolean/Dictionary/ListString/Reference [to a Const/Model]) and any nested elements (in the case of a Dictionary/List where, whilst we only support String keys, we need to know the value type):

Example from the Test Data:

```json
{
	"operations": {
		"GetImmediate": {
			"contentType": "application/json; charset=utf-8",
			"expectedStatusCodes": [
				200
			],
			"longRunning": false,
			"method": "GET",
			"requestObject": null,
			"resourceIdName": null,
			"responseObject": {
				"referenceName": "NestedItem",
				"type": "Reference"
			},
			"apiVersion": null,
			"uriSuffix": null,
			"fieldContainingPaginationDetails": null,
			"options": {}
		},
		"GetStringImmediate": {
			"contentType": "application/json; charset=utf-8",
			"expectedStatusCodes": [
				200
			],
			"longRunning": false,
			"method": "GET",
			"requestObject": null,
			"resourceIdName": null,
			"responseObject": {
				"referenceName": null,
				"type": "String"
			},
			"apiVersion": null,
			"uriSuffix": null,
			"fieldContainingPaginationDetails": null,
			"options": {}
		}
	},
	"metaData": {
		"resourceProvider": "Microsoft.Blah"
	}
}
```

